# Line-ending policy: LF in the index and in the worktree, on every platform.
# Ruling: halheinrich/backgammon#28.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Jellyfish .MAT export goldens are byte-exact fixtures. Measured
# (halheinrich/backgammon#166): MatExporter deliberately emits LF-only text
# (a '\n' constant; its doc bars StringBuilder.AppendLine for exactly this),
# and the committed golden is LF-only — 83 LF-terminated lines, zero CR bytes.
# `-text` is defense in depth for byte-exactness, not a CRLF fix: under the
# pinned `eol=lf` above no checkout would CRLF these anyway, but a fixture
# compared byte-for-byte must sit outside ALL EOL processing — index
# normalization at add time and any future checkout policy — so the bytes the
# test reads are always the bytes that were committed.
*.mat -text
